 "warnings": [
  "*** A THIRD DRAWING NUMBER APPEARS IN THIS SET: SN 62034. *** The structural sheets are S 62047, the architectural AR 61142, and the sanitary SN 62034 -- three separately numbered submissions for one house, all dated ม.ค. 2562. The drawing number is a submission id, never a project id.",
  "Ten sanitary sheets, SN-01 to SN-10, mapping to PNG 51-60 on the same +2 offset as the rest of the book.",
  "THE PIPE TABLE IS THE MOST QUANTIFIABLE THING HERE and it carries the falls, which no plan repeats: soil (S) at 1:100, waste (W), kitchen waste (K) and rainwater all at 1:50, vent (V) and cold water (CW) with no fall stated.",
  "PIPE CLASS SPLITS BY SERVICE, and getting it wrong is a real error: everything DRAINING is PVC class 8.5, but the potable cold-water line CW is class 13.5 -- the heavier wall. Both to มอก.17. External storm drainage is not PVC at all, it is off-the-shelf concrete pipe ('ท่อคอนกรีตท้องตลาด') sized 'ตามแบบ'.",
  "The legend runs to about 40 symbols in four columns. Two pairs share one abbreviation with different drawn symbols -- FD. (two floor-drain types), FCO. (two floor cleanout types) and AVC. (top-vent and side-vent caps) -- so the abbreviation alone does not identify the item; the drawn symbol does.",
  "ONE ITEM IN THE LEGEND IS NOT PLUMBING AT ALL: DC, a dry-chemical ABC fire extinguisher, 6A-20B 15 lbs to มอก.332. It is a real countable item that appears in no architectural schedule.",
  "SW ('ท่อระบายน้ำเสียรวม') and R ('ท่อระบายน้ำฝน') are in the legend but NOT in the pipe-type table, so they have no class or fall specified on this sheet."
